  "verbalization": "Acacetin 7-(2G-rhamnosyl)-rutinoside is implicated in the pathway leading to CD276 antigen through multiple indirect routes. The drug is identified as a target of KP-4 and Murrayaquinone A, both of which are themselves targets of CD276 antigen. This suggests a potential mechanism where Acacetin 7-(2G-rhamnosyl)-rutinoside may influence the activity of KP-4 or Murrayaquinone A, which in turn modulate CD276 antigen expression. The evidence is consistent with a regulatory or functional relationship, where the drug may act as a modulator of downstream targets that ultimately interact with CD276 antigen. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role in cellular signaling or immune response regulation, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
